Reason:
The bug occurs because the termination process does not wait for `libdecor` to finish its initialization if no windows were created. This leads to the premature destruction of the associated sync callback object, which can cause a segmentation fault when the code attempts to access uninitialized or invalid memory.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
while (!_glfw.wl.libdecor.ready)
    _glfwWaitEventsWayland();
```
```c
libdecor_unref(_glfw.wl.libdecor.context);
```
Reason:
The fix introduces a wait loop that ensures `libdecor` has completed its initialization before proceeding with the termination. This prevents the premature destruction of the sync callback object, thereby avoiding the segmentation fault during the termination process.

